# retroforge video codec links — /dev/video-enc0 for the hardware encoder; /dev/video-dec0 on SM6115 only.
#
# The SoCs' video block is a stateful V4L2 mem2mem device, driven by qcom-iris on every SoC we ship
# (SM6115 and SM4450 since 2026-11-23, kernel/patches/1095; venus before). Its nodes are
# /dev/videoN with N in probe order.
#
# The Steam UI's Chromium (libcef) decodes video through V4L2 only when /dev/video-dec0 exists.
# SM8250/SM8550/SM8650 get no decoder link, deliberately (user, 2026-10-29): there that path is
# worse than their CPU decode. The Steam UI ran four cores near 100% at 95 C on the KONKR Pocket FIT
# (SM8650) at its first sign-in, two of them its V4L2Dev threads; Nova-Deck measured it slower and
# ~2.5x the total CPU on SM8250 and no gain on SM8650 (its docs/video-decode.md), and ships no such
# link either. SM4450 gets none until someone measures it (user, 2026-11-23).
# The SM6115 gets one (2026-11-22), with two kernel patches, measured under venus and ported to
# iris for AR50_LITE (2026-11-23, not yet measured there). 1097: its frames are limited to 8160
# macroblocks (1920x1088), which it now reports, so Chromium sends larger video (Steam's 1920x1200
# startup movies) to software. 1098: its decoded frames are mapped cached; Chromium reads each one
# on the CPU, and uncached it showed 180-188 of 300 frames of a 1080p30 VP9 clip at 167-175% CPU,
# worse than software. With both, in Steam's UI on the MANGMI Air X: 297-298 of 300 frames, none
# dropped, 106-112% CPU, against software's 300 at 161-170%.
# The SM6115 is told apart by its platform device's modalias, which lists the node's compatibles
# ("of:Nvideo-codecT(null)Cqcom,sm6115-venusCqcom,qcm2290-venus"); the SM4450 shares only the
# qcm2290 fallback. Steam's Remote Play client (streaming_client, CV4L2Accel) probes
# /dev/video0..99 as well as video-dec0..99, so it finds the decoder with or without a link.
# The names are iris's video_device names (iris_probe.c); the nodes keep systemd's root:video 0660,
# and the session user is in `video`.
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTR{name}=="qcom-iris-encoder", SYMLINK+="video-enc0"
SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTR{name}=="qcom-iris-decoder", ATTRS{modalias}=="*Cqcom,sm6115-venusC*", SYMLINK+="video-dec0"
